.megaplan/initiatives/native-python-pipelines/research/native-python-pipelines-end-goal-megaplan-example.md:117:## Why this is the end goal
.megaplan/initiatives/native-python-pipelines/research/native-python-pipelines-end-goal-megaplan-example.md:121:- **Phases are ordinary async functions.** They are `@phase`-decorated only so the runtime knows which calls are checkpoint boundaries.
.megaplan/initiatives/native-python-pipelines/research/native-python-pipelines-end-goal-megaplan-example.md:122:- **Subloops are ordinary function calls.** `run_subpipeline(tiebreaker_pipeline, ...)` runs another `@pipeline` function in its own checkpoint scope.
.megaplan/initiatives/native-python-pipelines/research/native-python-pipelines-end-goal-megaplan-example.md:123:- **Overrides are invisible to the author.** The runtime intercepts `await gate(...)` and applies any active override before the model runs.
.megaplan/initiatives/native-python-pipelines/research/native-python-pipelines-end-goal-megaplan-example.md:124:- **Contracts come from types.** `Draft`, `Plan`, `Critique`, etc. are dataclasses or Pydantic models whose schemas are registered with the runtime.
.megaplan/initiatives/native-python-pipelines/research/native-python-pipelines-end-goal-megaplan-example.md:126:## What the runtime is doing
.megaplan/initiatives/native-python-pipelines/research/native-python-pipelines-end-goal-megaplan-example.md:130:1. The runtime persists the current local-variable snapshot.
.megaplan/initiatives/native-python-pipelines/research/native-python-pipelines-end-goal-megaplan-example.md:134:5. It stores the result and resumes the pipeline.
.megaplan/initiatives/native-python-pipelines/research/native-python-pipelines-end-goal-megaplan-example.md:136:If the process restarts, the runtime reloads the snapshot, fast-forwards to the last completed phase, and continues from the next `await`.
.megaplan/initiatives/native-python-pipelines/research/native-python-pipelines-end-goal-megaplan-example.md:138:## What this is not
.megaplan/initiatives/native-python-pipelines/research/native-python-pipelines-end-goal-megaplan-example.md:140:This is not the first step. To get here safely, the current plan proposes:
.megaplan/initiatives/native-python-pipelines/research/native-python-pipelines-end-goal-megaplan-example.md:142:1. Build the bridge so native functions compile to the existing graph executor.
.megaplan/initiatives/native-python-pipelines/research/native-python-pipelines-end-goal-megaplan-example.md:144:3. Only then build the native runtime underneath and switch hot-path execution to it.

