docs/arnold/megaplan-source-path-reconciliation.md:165:The `arnold/conformance/legacy_reference_allowlist.json` and `arnold/conformance/checks.py` contain references to `arnold/pipelines/megaplan` as **legacy allowlist entries**. These are intentional — the conformance system tracks legacy references to ensure they are not reintroduced as live code paths. They are **dead path gate entries**: they exist only to detect regressions. They are not migration targets and do not require updates during M1.
