docs/arnold/workflow-manifest-runtime-review/subagent-results/wave7/w7-01-end-to-end-behavior-parity.txt:16:The current tiebreaker resolves to `"iterate"` → critique → gate, and the gate CAN trigger tiebreaker again. This is a loop-back-into-loop, not a leaf subpipeline. M2 requires a "canonical Megaplan-shaped manifest fixture" but the plan language says "tiebreaker subpipeline/retry path" — singular. The fixture must exercise at least two tiebreaker rounds to prove the recursion isn't flattened.
