docs/arnold/workflow-manifest-runtime-review/subagent-results/wave9/w9-04-test-fixture-keepalive-attack.txt:11:**B. Whitelist rows acting as permanent keepalives.** M5 permits whitelisting only zero-public-surface internal coverage, with mandatory owner and expiry before M6. If a whitelisted pipeline, test root, generator script, or `test_*.py` is not burned down to migrate/delete before M6 closes, old execution paths survive under an "internal coverage" label. M6 correctly gates on this ("M6 cannot start while any M5 whitelist row still protects old native semantics"), but if that gate is checked by script output rather than human audit, a row reclassified at the last moment without actual migration is a false pass.
docs/arnold/workflow-manifest-runtime-review/subagent-results/wave9/w9-04-test-fixture-keepalive-attack.txt:21:**G. Editable-mode-only green CI.** The plan requires installed-wheel tests at M4 and M6. If conformance gates run only in editable mode — where old `arnold/pipelines/megaplan/` and `_pipeline/` directories resolve via local path — they pass. In a built wheel those directories are absent. If the wheel smoke is a separate step that doesn't block merge, deletion appears green while the wheel is broken.
docs/arnold/workflow-manifest-runtime-review/subagent-results/wave9/w9-04-test-fixture-keepalive-attack.txt:36:| 6 | Editable vs installed-wheel asymmetry | Add to M6 constraints: "Merge-result conformance gates must pass from a built wheel installed in a clean venv, not from an editable checkout. The editable checkout may be used for authoring but the gate is the wheel." |
docs/arnold/workflow-manifest-runtime-review/subagent-results/wave9/w9-04-test-fixture-keepalive-attack.txt:40:| 10 | Manifest amendment protocol bypass | Add to M6 Done Criteria: "Any manifest/kernel contract change discovered during M4/M5/M6 must be recorded in `workflow-manifest-amendments.md` with a version bump and must back-propagate to M1/M2/M3 contract tests. M6 cannot close with an amendment version newer than the one all conformance tests assert against." |
docs/arnold/workflow-manifest-runtime-review/subagent-results/wave9/w9-04-test-fixture-keepalive-attack.txt:60:7. **Allowlist burn-down with dynamic-proof:** Every conformance allowlist entry is either removed or re-chartered with dynamic-import proof of zero contact with deleted surfaces.
