docs/arnold/workflow-manifest-runtime-review/subagent-results/wave9/w9-09-agent-capability-runtime-attack.txt:7:**2. Adapter internals not exercised by conformance.** M3 requires `arnold.agent` adapters satisfy neutral dispatch protocols without product imports. But an adapter class could internally `from arnold.pipelines.megaplan.schemas import MegaplanSignal` in a method body that conformance tests never call. AST scans on the adapter module pass because nothing at the module level imports deleted surfaces; the import is conditional or lazy. M6 must require *execution-coverage* of all adapter registration paths, not just static scans.
docs/arnold/workflow-manifest-runtime-review/subagent-results/wave9/w9-09-agent-capability-runtime-attack.txt:17:**7. Generated artifacts with stale provenance.** M5 requires regenerated skills/docs to pass semantic checks. If the regeneration step itself produces correct output but the generator code still contains `import deleted_surface` (because the generator isn't run during conformance scans, only its output is), the scan passes. M6 criterion 13 checks regeneration diffs but must also AST-scan the generator scripts themselves.
docs/arnold/workflow-manifest-runtime-review/subagent-results/wave9/w9-09-agent-capability-runtime-attack.txt:41:2. **Coverage report over adapter registration** showing every `arnold.agent` adapter method, every product handler registration, and every callback recovery path was executed in the conformance suite with import tracing enabled.
