docs/arnold/workflow-manifest-runtime-review/subagent-results/load-bearing-questions/lbq-09-clean-break-proof.txt:33:None. The plan is unusually tight on this point. M6's scope goes beyond the written answer in useful ways (e.g., dynamic-import tracing covers `importlib`, `__getattr__`, `eval`, `exec`; conformance-allowlist burn-down; final manifest-identity ledger), but these are elaborations, not corrections. The answer's core claim — that the clean break is proven by absence across all artifact classes from installed artifacts — is the organizing principle of M6.
